cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Erdős Problem #1144: A Lean 4 proof of almost-sure positive unboundedness"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-06
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - given-names: "Sigurd"
    family-names: "Høystad"
repository-code: "https://github.com/saasom/Erdos1144"
url: "https://github.com/saasom/Erdos1144/releases/tag/v1.0.0"
abstract: >-
  A kernel-checked Lean 4 proof that the partial sums of a completely
  multiplicative random function with independent fair signs on the primes,
  normalized by the square root of the cutoff, have almost surely infinite
  positive limsup. The public theorem has no hypotheses and its axiom
  dependencies are exactly propext, Classical.choice, and Quot.sound.
keywords:
  - "Lean 4"
  - "formal proof"
  - "probabilistic number theory"
  - "random multiplicative functions"
  - "Erdős problems"
